of 13 million people, the roads are navigable, and the old parts of the city quietly do what they've always done: serve breakfast that's been perfected over decades, keep parks open for the joggers and the chess players and the people who just need an hour of quiet. If you're an early riser, this city will reward you for it."}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.4rem","fontWeight":600,"marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"Bangalore Morning Spots Worth Waking Up For"}],["$","ol",null,{"style":{"paddingLeft":"1.25rem","lineHeight":"1.9"},"children":["$L7","$L8","$L9","$La","$Lb","$Lc","$Ld"]}],"$Le","$Lf","$L10"]}],null,"$L11"]}],{},null,false]},null,false]},null,false]},null,false],"$L12",false]],"m":"$undefined","G":["$13",[]],"s":false,"S":true}
