7:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"CTR (Central Tiffin Room)"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Malleshwaram"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"If there is a platonic ideal of a Bangalore morning, it involves a masala dosa from CTR. This place has been operating since 1920 and the dosa batter recipe has not changed. It opens at 7:30 AM, the queue starts forming at 7:15. The dosas come out so fast it almost seems like a performance. Go hungry, go early, don't bother looking at the menu — just ask for the benne masala dosa."}]]}]
8:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Cubbon Park, Gate 1"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Kasturba Road, CBD"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Enter at Gate 1 on Kasturba Road between 6 and 7 AM and you get the park in its best form: the light comes through the trees at a low angle, the mist hasn't fully cleared yet, and the only people around are regulars who know what they have. The park has over 6,000 trees — including some specimens over 150 years old. Walk slowly and look up."}]]}]
9:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Nandi Hills Viewpoint"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— ~60 km north, Chikballapur district"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Yes, it requires leaving by 4:30 AM. Yes, it's worth it. At the top, Nandi Hills sits above a sea of clouds that burns off slowly as the sun comes up. The fort ruins at the summit give the whole thing an unexpectedly ancient feeling. Bring a jacket — it can be 10°C at the viewpoint even when it's 25°C in Bangalore."}]]}]
a:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Ulsoor Lake Walking Path"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Ulsoor, Central Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"The lake path opens at 5:30 AM and the first hour belongs entirely to the serious walkers and the birds. Ulsoor has a healthy resident population of painted storks, open-billed storks, and kingfishers. The full loop is about 2.5 km. After the walk, the small tea stall at the north gate does good cutting chai."}]]}]
b:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Vidyarthi Bhavan"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Gandhi Bazaar, Basavanagudi"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Open only on weekends and only until about noon. The masala dosas here are the colour of old copper and arrive in batches — the waiter brings them as they come off the griddle, not to order. The ghee usage is aggressive and correct. This place has been open since 1943. It is always worth the wait."}]]}]
c:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Bannerghatta Road Sunrise Point"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Bannerghatta, South Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"The stretch of Bannerghatta Road leading toward the national park has an underused viewpoint where you can watch the sun come up over the Deccan plateau. It's a working road so you'll have some truck noise, but on weekdays between 6 and 7 AM it's quiet enough. Good for motorcyclists who want a short dawn ride with a payoff."}]]}]
d:["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sankey Tank Morning Circuit"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Sadashivanagar, North Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"A 1.6 km tank in one of Bangalore's most pleasant old neighbourhoods. The morning circuit is popular with the local bungalow residents and the light on the water is especially good in winter. Less crowded than Ulsoor, better maintained than most other lakes. Bring your binoculars if you have them — egrets and herons are regulars."}]]}]
e:["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.4rem","fontWeight":600,"margin":"2rem 0 1rem"},"children":"Why Bangalore Mornings Hit Different"}]
f:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8","marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"There's a version of this city that most people never see because they're asleep for it. The old Bangalore — Malleshwaram, Basavanagudi, Rajajinagar — is most itself in the morning. Flower vendors setting up on the pavement, the smell of jasmine and ghee, filter coffee in steel tumblers, newspapers. It's not nostalgia, it's just still happening, every day, if you show up early enough."}]
10:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8"},"children":"Set an alarm. It's worth it."}]
